{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791044035,"nonce":"q3NX5sGgOXxBFlCwoEpEGrH4A2A=","title":"Short bold text wraps mid-word at 1x","message":"In tools/snapshot/scenes/Filters.hx, the label \"Card\" (text-xs font-bold, in a w-24 flex-col items-center card) draws as \"Car\" / \"d\" at scale 1 and on one line at scale 2. The break is mid-word although wrapping is by word, so the renderer's line is wider than the box Taffy laid out from the measurer's width by more than text::prepare's allowance of one layout unit.\n\nLikely cause: the renderer's glyph advances at raster size are rounded per glyph, and across a short bold word at 12px the rounding exceeds 1 px, while the measurer measures unrounded (or rounded differently); at scale 2 the same rounding is half as large in layout units. To check: measure \"Card\" bold 12px through the measurer and through renderer.prepare_text_with_style at scale 1 and compare widths.\n\nPossible fixes: measure with the renderer's own rounding (share one registry and one path, init_text_measurer_with_registry), or wrap only when the text is wider than the box by more than the rounding can explain (e.g. half a pixel per glyph), or never break inside a word that the measurer placed on one line.","files":null}]}